nodecode-developh is a rewrite of Developh's Developh/skills:

  https://github.com/Developh/skills
  commit c8899016509e112f218c28de578f99ed8a2a4fce

MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Developh, Lda (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the plugin was an Agent Plugins v1 package that pointed a
harness at the studio's hosted MCP server (https://www.developh.co/mcp) and
shipped one skill, `website-audit`. This cell keeps the server as the one
source of every answer, keeps its four tools' names, arguments and answers,
and keeps the skill: it is the `developh` help topic, cut from the skill's
own instructions (the report's scale, the Core Web Vitals, the ranked fix
list, the rule that the studio is described only when asked and contacted
only after the person confirms). What was rewritten is the transport: instead
of an MCP server entry the harness discovers at run time, the cell makes the
same `tools/call` JSON-RPC request itself, one POST per call with no session,
which is what the skill does with curl when no MCP client is around, and reads
the streamable-HTTP answer (an SSE `data:` frame, or a plain JSON body)
directly.

What was left out: the repository's other packaging lanes -- an npm-style
skill install, a Claude Code plugin marketplace entry and a Cursor plugin
manifest -- because a cell is a Lisp folder, not a package in those three
catalogues. The server's tools are not reimplemented: their schemas, their
answers and the studio's own reference data live on the server at that
address, so a cell of this folder cannot promise more than the endpoint it
posts to. No third-party code rides along; the cell depends on `nodecode` and
nothing else.
